{"agent":"recover-2f","data":{"budget":"","claim":"A signal-killed review records the finished chunks (bug B982d306cc8) but a re-run re-sends EVERY chunk. Checkpointing the cut's identity (reviewer, diff_sha, chunks_total, max_chunk_chars) the moment the runner knows it lets the next run resume from the next unreviewed chunk of the SAME cut.","falsifier":"The resumed run re-sends an already-reviewed chunk (the test asserts chunk 1's marker appears exactly once across both runs), or the partial record lacks diff_sha/chunks_total/reviewer so a resume cannot name the cut.","item":"DX-review-chunk-checkpoint","mechanism":"ddflow/services/review/runner.review already computes diff_sha/chunks_total/max_chunk_chars after splitting the diff; wire an on_plan callback that writes one plan line into the reply file, surface it in the terminated gate's evidence, and have scope._scope resume via _resume_of_terminated, which reuses _rerun_scope to validate the cut matches before picking only the missing chunk numbers.","probe":"tests/test_review_checkpoint.py::test_a_killed_review_resumes_from_the_next_chunk -- kill mid-round with chunk 1 done, then resume and assert seen.log holds x_marker_zz exactly once and evidence reviewed == [1,2]","probe_output":"running via the ci gate (scoped selection reaches tests/test_review_checkpoint.py and tests/test_review_checkpoint_kill.py); expected pass","question":"How does a ddflow review resume after being killed mid-round, and what does it need to skip the chunks already answered?","sources":["ddflow/api/review/runner.py","ddflow/api/review/reviewers.py","ddflow/api/review/scope.py","tests/test_review_checkpoint_kill.py"],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"ebfb8262f01b348a2f28a16ef","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":153108,"schema":1,"subject":"Rb0a7d7b8d4","ts":"2026-11-08T06:16:40.975414Z"}
