{"agent":"recover-2f","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test never inspects the actual finished chunk’s outcome/finding. After the first kill it checks only `evidence[\"reviewed\"] == [1]`, and after resume it checks only `evidence[\"reviewed\"] == [1, 2]` and that `x_marker_zz` was not re-sent. An implementation that checkpointed the chunk *index* `1` but discarded the replied `FINDING HIGH x.py:1` payload would satisfy every assertion, yet the gate would silently lose the x.py finding — the exact “persist each finished chunk’s outcome” behavior this test claims to pin. The test should assert the chunk-1 finding content is present after the kill and still present in the final gate after resume.","digest":"b951b8d3f53243e8","family":"deepseek","location":"tests/test_review_checkpoint.py:test_a_killed_review_resumes_from_the_next_chunk","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_review_checkpoint.py:test_a_killed_review_resumes_from_the_next_chunk"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"A rejected explicit chunk rerun is treated as “no rerun” and can be replaced by a terminated-run resume. After `if a[\"chunks\"]`, a string from `_rerun_scope` is stored in `why` and `rerun` is set to `None`; the new `if rerun is None` then calls `_resume_of_terminated` with no check that `a[\"chunks\"]` was empty and without clearing `why`. Given `a[\"chunks\"] == [1]` and `_rerun_scope` returning an error (chunk 1 already reviewed, out of range, or otherwise not a valid rerun) while a PARTIAL record still has missing chunk 3 that `_rerun_scope` accepts, the function returns that error in `why` and a resume scope for chunk 3 in `rerun`. Callers that honor `rerun` review the wrong chunks; callers that honor `why` drop a resume the two-line-above contract (`rerun` set ⇒ `why` empty) no longer describes.","digest":"184532993e448610","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/review/scope.py:_resume_of_terminated call site","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/review/scope.py:_resume_of_terminated call site"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`seen` is not reset between the kill and the resume, and the slow reviewer appends the chunk body before it sleeps. After a kill, `seen` already contains `y_marker_zz` from the terminated invocation, so `assert \"y_marker_zz\" in got` is true even when the second `review` never calls the reviewer. A resume that only rewrites `evidence[\"reviewed\"]` to `[1, 2]` from the checkpoint (without sending chunk 2, and without re-sending `x_marker_zz`) satisfies every assert in `test_a_killed_review_resumes_from_the_next_chunk`, including `got.count(\"x_marker_zz\") == 1`. The same log also never checks that chunk 1’s stored finding is still on the gate, so “keep the finished outcome” is untested.","digest":"b5d278fb7fe42603","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_review_checkpoint.py:128","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_review_checkpoint.py:128"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":13789,"diff_sha":"1384b491527ba8f3264bac0c9059d01c77e38d00ac0c6d2e5481ffc040d44ded","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/DX-review-chunk-checkpoint","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":144.3,"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"62d501b7f37019d6","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-review-chunk-checkpoint.critic.grok-4.7.20261108T062915Z-c7dc56f6.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"1e7c7e9e45ee732b3a998a4e8e7627ecd593a208","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/review/gate.py":"100644 58f963d27b3ff50b8884e144d7f2d757a6aa00c5","ddflow/api/review/reviewers.py":"100644 96b6a411eeeadc01fb84f39bfe76564db3898c02","ddflow/api/review/run.py":"100644 b383b1438783d